WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:04.400
Waver

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.550
Love letter?

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.010
Yes!

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:22.560
I have decided to share my feelings
with Kaguya!

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.260
Please, give me your guidance!

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.190
Guidance?

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.740
You know, it feels more like
a letter of challenge than a love letter.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.320
The Great Passage

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:56.660
A quiet dreamlike morning, the madder red sky
shines through the window and reflects on my pen

00:00:56.790 --> 00:01:02.800
The vivid clatter of the night,
I wander between cities like a cat

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:09.440
Deep thoughts, flexible conception;
foreseeable aspirations, distant memories; unruly hair

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:16.080
Narrow mind, large circle of friends;
long silence, short greeting;tone of voice

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:22.380
The light in our eyes that differ from each other,
traces of friendship that’s not in the treaty

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:28.690
In the ocean that sweeps the sand of eternity

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:35.660
Swept and sunk in the waves with sparse
opposites and similarities

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:42.170
Clashing and exact opposites become
resolved and connected

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:48.710
Reference, conclusion; I’ll gather words that have
scattered over many months and years

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:55.180
The fragrant sea breeze;
the connection that rests on the seashore, become one.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:13.330
"Dear madam, the bitter throes of winter
are almost at hand.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.340
I pray that life has found you well."

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.200
What the hell is this?

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.770
It's way too stiff.

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:23.640
Even corporate public apologies
aren't this ceremonial.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.580
Is it bad?

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.720
It would be very helpful if you could
give me some concrete advice.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.520
Advice, huh?

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.790
I'll read through it later.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.430
Thank you.

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.700
Good morning.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.270
Good morning.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.370
Wait, Matsumoto-sensei, the monthly
meeting isn't scheduled today, is it?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.740
- We're expecting "that" to arrive today.
- "That"?

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.680
"That."

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.950
Has "that" not arrived yet?

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.910
"That" has not arrived yet.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.650
I see.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.220
It hasn't, has it?

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.490
I cannot wait for "that."

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.860
Yes, I cannot wait to see "that."

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.690
What's this "that"?

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:14.390
You know. "That."

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:21.200
This is
the Dictionary Editorial Department.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:22.470
Yes?

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.640
Yes.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:28.270
Yes. Understood.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.580
Nishioka, Director Yamashita wants you
in the conference room right away.

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.680
The director does?

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.280
So it's the time of reckoning.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:40.550
I figured he'd come say something soon.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:46.630
We've taken a lot of actions
to save Daitokai after all.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:50.830
Anyway, I'm just going to
go get this over with.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:07.280
Conference Room

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.560
- Oh, sorry, sorry, sorry.
- It's okay.

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.960
I ran into the managing director.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.900
He's a real talker, you know?

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.530
- You wanted to see m--
- Daitokai.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:30.970
I heard you're working hard.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:36.310
And you got Hokuto University's
Prof. Shinohara to be a contributor.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:39.580
Now how did you manage to
convince a man like him?

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:41.380
I bet that was pretty hard.

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:45.490
I suppose so. Well, dictionaries
are the face of a publisher.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.490
I agree with you on that!

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.290
So we've been talking.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.530
We want you to
use your talents elsewhere.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:58.400
So we're transferring you
to the PR Department.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.440
Good for you! You first applied to be
in the PR Department, right?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:04.800
Yes, but...

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.770
I've already talked to
the PR Department director.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.940
We'll move you in the spring.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.550
But we've just started editing Daitokai.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.420
I appreciate the offer but...

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:17.950
Oh, I don't think so.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:22.090
Weren't you prepared to pay the price
for everything you've been doing?

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.530
Oh, and one more thing.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.570
You'll also be revising the Genbu
Japanese Learning Dictionary

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.470
while you edit Daitokai.

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:40.970
You know how that dictionary is showing
strong sales in the grade school market.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:44.640
It will sell even more
with a revised edition.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:45.880
But...

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:50.350
Sorry, the executive director
is expecting me. You know how he is.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.950
Well, thanks again!

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.370
- Then we will go with this.
- Understood.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:14.070
Nishioka-san?

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:18.850
What did Director Yamashita
want to see you about?

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.960
Genbu Japanese Learning Dictionary

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:32.930
Revising the Genbu Japanese
Learning Dictionary.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:36.860
But we just did a big revision on it
last year.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.930
He's telling us to earn the money
to make Daitokai ourselves.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:43.140
What are we going to do?

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.140
We can't.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:48.110
We cannot possibly revise
some other dictionary

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:52.010
while creating one with over
200,000 words from the ground up.

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.620
We should just be concentrating
on Daitokai.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.720
But we have to do it nonetheless.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:06.530
The experience from this revision will
surely help us with Daitokai in some way.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:10.030
This is your first time creating a dictionary,
Majime-san.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.630
Instead of learning with Daitokai,

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:17.500
it would be better if you built experience
with the Learning Dictionary first.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.610
Okay.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.750
Was that his only condition?

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.480
Well, yes.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:34.020
I figured that shark would've demanded
one or two more things.

00:07:34.150 --> 00:07:38.620
We'll need to redo the schedule
incorporating the revision work as well.

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:39.760
Nishioka-san--

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.830
Oh, no! I had an appointment
with Prof. Matsuda from Hama University!

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.770
All right, I'm off to my meeting.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:48.670
- Okay.
- Take care.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:15.830
PR Department

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.160
Yes. We'll touch base tomorrow.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:20.130
Yes. Have a nice day.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.140
- Miyoshi.
- Yes?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:29.740
I heard you went to the same university as
Nishioka from the Dictionary Department.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:33.010
Yes, although Nishioka-san
was ahead of me.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.950
What's he like?

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.520
I'm sorry, we didn't know each other
very well.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:40.120
Oh, I see.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.790
Did something happen
with Nishioka-san?

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:46.790
He's going to be transferring
to our department.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:54.600
I can't look at him right now.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.240
Not when he makes that face.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:02.840
Just when I thought I could start
enjoying dictionary making...

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.810
I thought I finally found my place.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:09.580
Just like Majime, Araki-san
and Matsumoto-sensei.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:11.280
I thought I...

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:17.260
Ah, well. I guess this means
I wasn't cut out for it after all.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:21.630
Now then...

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.630
Where should I go?

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:38.190
I'm like a middle-aged man
who's just been downsized.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:44.760
I wonder what's going to happen
to the Dictionary Department.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:49.160
Will Majime really be able to go on?

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.200
This is stupid.

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.400
Thinking about this isn't going to help.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:06.080
- Yeah?
- Ma-kun?

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.950
You never call during work.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:11.790
What's up?

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:18.260
I thought maybe we could
go out to lunch sometime.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.700
Together?

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:23.070
What if someone from work sees us?

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.340
Well, we can deal with that
if it comes up.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.400
I'd like to talk...

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:32.040
Talk? What's that supposed to mean?

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.080
We can talk at home--

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:39.210
Hello? Ma-kun. Can you hear me?

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:41.350
Hello?

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.860
Sorry. I'm busy with outside meetings
right now.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:50.730
I've got a few more to go to.

00:10:50.860 --> 00:10:52.860
Oh, okay.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:54.860
Ah, before I forget,

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:58.230
it seems I'm being transferred
to the PR Department.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:00.200
R-- Really?

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:05.170
Although, it won't be for a while. I'll be
counting on you to show me the ropes.

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:07.380
Well, talk to you later.

00:11:07.710 --> 00:11:09.980
Okay. Later then.

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:15.750
I can't believe she checked in on me.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:31.200
One, two, three, four.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:33.470
Fifteen pages?!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.900
What was he thinking?

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:42.950
"Dear madam, the bitter throes of winter
are almost at hand.

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:47.050
I pray that life has found you well.

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:53.760
Snow, sun, mountain pass..."

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.360
Who could read this thing?!

00:11:57.490 --> 00:12:00.000
Why would he write
a Chinese poem here?

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:56.320
I guess I did promise to give him advice...

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:12.030
I'm back!

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:17.310
Sensei, what do you think about this?

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:20.840
I believe this typeface is better.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:24.510
I think this line spacing is easier to read.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.280
Welcome back.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:29.520
So I gather the sample pages arrived.

00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:33.590
They've been like that for two hours
with just the few pages we have.

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:37.230
I don't know what they'll do
when the rest arrives.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:43.570
Don't you think these white numbers
on the black dots are hard to read?

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:47.500
I thought it'd come through more clearly.
This probably won't work.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:54.010
Why does our mushroom picture
look so terrible? It looks poisonous.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:56.510
I drew that.

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:58.580
I wanted to check the positioning.

00:13:58.910 --> 00:14:02.350
Oh, that's a mushroom?
I thought it was a strawberry.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:05.590
That really hurts, Matsumoto-sensei.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:09.590
- Nishioka!
- Welcome back.

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:11.990
Don't give me that.

00:14:12.590 --> 00:14:14.430
What is wrong with you people?

00:14:14.560 --> 00:14:19.130
Oh, look at the time. Sensei, why don't we
continue this over soba noodles?

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:20.370
Good idea!

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.670
What about the rest of you?

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:24.570
- Yes.
- Yes, please.

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:28.040
Oh, sorry.
I have to leave right after again.

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:29.380
I see.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.260
I'll go after tidying up a bit.

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:47.100
All right, see you there.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:52.300
Majime-san, let's discuss
the number symbols at the restaurant.

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:54.000
Okay.

00:14:55.140 --> 00:14:58.310
Have you already started
the revision work?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:14:59.980
Yes.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:01.440
Of course you have.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:03.950
We want to publish Daitokai after all.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.150
Yes.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:06.580
But...

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:10.620
I'd like to do a good job with the revision
as well.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:16.220
We'll need to schedule meetings
for the revision work too.

00:15:16.590 --> 00:15:18.230
Yes, we will.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:19.560
Also...

00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:28.540
There were a lot of parts
I didn't understand.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:32.270
But I got that you were serious.
I think it's fine.

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.980
Why don't you just hand it to her
like bam!

00:15:35.110 --> 00:15:37.150
Like bam?

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.480
Or maybe like wham!

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:44.250
What I'm trying to say, it's all about
what feels right at the time.

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:49.060
You know,

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:52.130
you could stand to be more confident.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:55.530
An earnest guy like you,

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:59.200
everything is bound to work out.

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:03.070
And I'll help you however I can.

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.180
Oda

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:13.150
Hello. I'm Nishioka from Genbu.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:16.790
I haven't finished the manuscript yet.

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:20.090
Oh, that's all right.
I was just in the neighborhood.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:21.790
I'm sorry if I'm interrupting.

00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:24.330
It's all right. I was just finishing.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:27.600
Did your wife pack you that?
I'm jealous.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:29.600
Oh, uhh...

00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:34.540
Anyway, I've heard a strange rumor.

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:36.810
- Rumor?
- Genbu Books Publishing

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:40.140
is not enthusiastic
about compiling a new dictionary.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:41.780
It could even be canceled.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:45.750
How ridiculous.
That's not the case at all.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:48.080
Where did you hear that?

00:16:48.220 --> 00:16:49.480
If that were the case,

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:52.720
then I wouldn't be asking you
for a manuscript.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:54.590
Well, that's fine, then.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:59.530
It's a little awkward to bring up, but
dictionary writing isn't exactly lucrative.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.330
Of course I will give you my best work,
but I am a busy person.

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:07.840
- I don't want to waste my time on uncer--
- I can assure you.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:11.570
The Dictionary Editorial Department
has some new excellent recruits.

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:13.580
There is no need to worry!

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:18.350
And just look!

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:20.650
That is wonderful!

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.680
See how well it cuts?

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:26.090
That is amazing!

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:28.660
But I'm sure it's expensive.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:31.660
But it isn't! We will also throw in a--

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:54.280
Sup?

00:17:54.780 --> 00:17:56.380
Ma-kun?

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:12.400
- Come on, Ma-kun!
- All right, I'll do it.

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.640
Until I get transferred,

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:18.840
I'm going to do
absolutely everything I can

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:22.340
before I go.

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:44.570
Ah, that was a nice bath.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.200
What are you doing, Micchan?

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.910
Um, I'm just...

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.610
Be sure to turn out the lights
and lock the door.

00:18:58.750 --> 00:18:59.750
Okay.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:03.790
Oh, and I haven't seen Tora-san today.

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:06.220
Could you feed him if you see him?

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:08.490
Well, good night.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:09.860
Good night.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:30.480
I'm home--!

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:33.750
Micchan.

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:37.620
What are you doing?

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:39.960
I'm sorry I startled you.

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:49.760
Please read this.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.570
These are my feelings!

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.910
Well, good night.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.630
To Kaguya Hayashi

00:20:24.400 --> 00:20:29.900
Waver: To drift about
My heart was lost like a floating boat

00:20:34.010 --> 00:20:44.520
Hey, it’s a full moon tonight

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:55.530
I speak to you softly as you sleep

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:07.380
Your gestures, attitude, and way of life

00:21:07.840 --> 00:21:14.080
Mean so much to me more than any word

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:19.920
So please stay the way you are

00:21:20.660 --> 00:21:26.030
I & I = You & I
Feel it

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:31.500
Here with you, forever by your side

00:21:31.670 --> 00:21:44.410
I’ve loved you from the day we met

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:54.460
Honestly...

00:21:54.890 --> 00:21:57.630
Majime would write a love letter like this.

00:21:58.430 --> 00:22:01.600
I'd better make a copy just in case.

00:22:02.100 --> 00:22:06.130
You never know how this might help
with Daitokai one day.
